  "description": "The identity an MCP server's identify callback (Python identify, Go Identify) returns, and what its events carry. user_id, anonymous_id, account_id and oauth_client_id: a string is trimmed of Unicode White_Space and then capped at 256 code points, once, so a cap that ends in white space keeps it; blank is absent. token_scopes: string entries only, each trimmed and capped at 64 code points, blank entries dropped, then at most 100. user_id and anonymous_id are the event's userId and anonymousId; account_id, oauth_client_id and token_scopes are mcp_client_seen properties (account_id and oauth_client_id also on mcp_tool_called). auth_method and country are short labels: trimmed the same way and capped at 64 code points; they are mcp_client_seen properties (auth_method also on mcp_tool_called).",
